# Scenario cancel-signal-twice (review WR-04, D-21, D-23): outcome cancelled, exit 12;
# host-dependent (signals). As cancel-signal, but run with --self-signal-count 2: ivs-run raises
# SIGINT twice in the cancel check after slice 1 (no racing signal, no sleep). The handler must
# survive the first signal (BSD signal() semantics, also on glibc), so the second is just another
# cancel request and the run still ends cancelled with a report, not killed by the signal.
# expect-detail: signal step=1
ivss 1
id cancel-signal-twice
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-cpu-1.ivsc
run-to 4000 cpu-cycles stop halted
assert halted == yes
